(D4 — Discrepancy 4 repro, the quiet sibling of D3: a loop-expansion
 clause whose collection was a MAP used to be accepted with no diagnostic
 and printed one garbage value per entry (0, 0, 3) instead of erroring; a
 BUFFER collection behaved the same way (6513249, 0, 0 -- 0x636261 is
 "abc" read as a list header). The manual's supported-collection list
 (LANGUAGE.md:2803-2806) contains neither.
 **RESOLVED — fixed by vox #49 (0.4.8+), the same check that fixed D3.**
 Both clauses are now compile errors, each with a kind-specific hint:
   scores is a map - iterate `scores's keys` or `scores's values`
   sink is a buffer - `each ... from` walks a list, a range, or
   `arguments's all`
 The caret points at the DECLARATION of the offending collection rather
 than at the loop clause; see also Discrepancy 10 (`D10.vox`).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D4.vox -o p && ./p
